keywords:
  - soil erosion
  - cover factor
  - RUSLE
  - MUSLE
  - Sentinel-2
  - NDVI
  - aggregate stability
  - soil organic carbon
  - Sri Lanka
  - Uma Oya
abstract: >-
  Field measurements at 14 sites (7 managed vs less-disturbed pairs) in the Uma Oya basin, Sri Lanka, 5-7 October 2026:
  30-point cover tape, slake-test aggregate stability, handheld NIR soil-carbon predictions at four depths, and
  metadata-stripped cover photos with derived cover statistics. Includes the field-calibrated Sentinel-2 NDVI cover
  factor curve (C = exp(0.3404 - 3.8457 NDVI), NDVI 0.407-0.848) and a frozen snapshot of the Storm Model engine
  (MIT) with a one-command script reproducing the basin sediment yields 2,073, 1,850 and 119 t km-2 yr-1.
  Site positions are generalised to a 0.002-degree grid to protect private landholdings.
